A||||9||ChadMan||How much $$$ for a good paint job?||||1||
Z||000000||ChadMan||12-08-1999||02:43 PM||||Like most Fiero lovers, I have taken pains to keep my 88 Coupe looking good.  But the original Med Red Metallic paint is losing its luster on the hood, roof and deck lid, and is starting to fade in two spots.<P>How much should I expect to pay for a good paint job?  I don't expect a perfect finish, but I want something equivalent to what you find on a brand new car that will hold up to at least 5-7 years of handwashing, waxing, and outdoor storage.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||12-08-1999||03:14 PM||||You can get one of those 199.95 paint jobs, but you get what you pay for. Expect to spend $650 or more for a good paint job.||||reg||14
Z||000002||deceler8||12-08-1999||03:35 PM||||Let's see...four cans of Sunset Red Rust-Oleum, four pack of 1000 grit paper, masking tape, newspapers...<P>I'd say $25. <P>Just kidding, although I did use Sunset Red Rust-Oleum to paint the wheels on my car and it is a perfect match for the red paint on my car. <P>If your damage is localized, it is possible to paint just those areas that need it and mask off the rest. I've done that with my roof that was fading and you'd be hard pressed to tell.||||reg||10
Z||000003||batboy||12-08-1999||04:09 PM||||If a reputable body shop does the work and it's done right, expect to pay well over $1,000 depending on how much repair work needs to be done.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||12-08-1999||06:11 PM||||One thing you can do to save you $$$ in the labor area, is to do a lot of the prep work yourself. i.e. sanding, filling dents(for steel bodied cars), rust.  I've heard of people just taking the body panels off their cars, doing all the prep work themselves, and just have a paint shop paint the panels.  Saves quite a bit of money I've heard.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Gokart||12-08-1999||07:56 PM||||I painted my 1st Fiero back in 95 twice! The first time didn't come out too swell cause I rushed it. The 2nd time after learning from my mistakes came out sweet! I painted it raspberry red mettalic and the total cost was under $300.00! About $200.00 for paint and $50.00 to rent the compressor plus supplies. If you do it yourself just take your time and sand and mask to perfection! Good luck!||||reg||12
Z||000006||loafer87gt||12-08-1999||07:58 PM||||You guys down south have it made. I have been getting some prices from stores up here in Canada and the cheapest quote I have got yet was $2900 bucks to get it repainted the factory red colour. Its almost worthwhile driving down there to do all my mods to my car as it seems like everything is way more expensive up here (rims, tires, engine parts, etc..) Oh well, at least our beer rocks!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-09-1999||12:14 AM||||batboy is right-I got a quote just last week on a fairly stock color (not a red).  $1100 if there was no body damage.  Just remember that the reds cost more money.  The body shop also told me that the heavy metals cost more, too.  I don't know what a heavy metal paint is.  Maybe AC/DC blue or Motley Crue green? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||12-09-1999||07:37 AM||||My only guess would be the different metal flake counts in the paint.  A couple of years ago, I had my car(before the Fiero) repainted.  I stuck with the stock color,and the paint shop guys said the colors that fade the fastest are the ones with the highest matallic flake contents. They are also the pricier paints if I remember correctly. Pricing here in ohio was averaging $1200 and up for what I wanted.  Well, I took care of all the prep work, sanding,etc, and it only cost me $750 to get the $1,500 paint job. It looked great.||||reg||1
Z||000009||ChadMan||12-09-1999||08:48 AM||||Thanks, you guys.  I see no point in painting my Coupe until I have a house with off-street parking, but it's nice to know about what it will cost me.||||reg||1
